data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Both work exactly like any other unmanaged type with `stackalloc`:

```csharp
Span<nint>  signed   = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> unsigned = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

The test confirmed reading/writing elements works correctly. On this 64-bit system, `nint` is 8 bytes. One minor note: `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context since the size is platform-dependent, but `stackalloc` itself works in safe code when assigned to a `Span`.
